================================================================================
## Let local setup create the venv when PATH python3 is Apple 3.9
================================================================================

Context: `./scripts/start.sh` reported "Virtual environment not found" and ran
setup, which then aborted because `/usr/bin/python3` is macOS 3.9. The venv
was never created. uv was already on PATH and can provision CPython >= 3.11
(`requires-python` in pyproject.toml). Local preflight now treats uv as the
runtime interpreter source; setup installs uv before that check.

Changes:

1. scripts/_internal/_deploy-preflight.sh
   Pass local-dev Python when uv is present even if PATH python3 is 3.9;
   require PATH python3 >= 3.11 only when uv is missing.
2. scripts/setup.sh
   Install uv before the --local preflight, then `uv venv`.
3. tests/units/scripts/test_local_dev_python_preflight.py
   Cover old PATH python3 with/without uv, and PATH 3.11 without uv.
4. docs/deployment.md
   Note that Apple python3 3.9 is acceptable when uv is on PATH.
5. docs/getting-started.md
   Document uv-provisioned CPython and the setup order.

Modified files:
- scripts/_internal/_deploy-preflight.sh
- scripts/setup.sh
- tests/units/scripts/test_local_dev_python_preflight.py
- docs/deployment.md
- docs/getting-started.md
- changelogs/v0.9.2/benoitcayladbx_2026-10-30.log

Tests: uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario" → 9629 passed, 326 skipped, 8 deselected, 40 warnings in 105.42s

